eneral-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Larry Rhoden (R) is running."]}, "overview": "South Dakota's governor race pits incumbent Republican Larry Rhoden, running for his first full term, against Democrat Dan Ahlers. The state's partisan lean favors Republicans by roughly fifteen points, and no public polls of the general election are available. All seven expert ratings call the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket give Rhoden about a 97 percent chance of winning.\n\nThe campaign has centered on affordability, education, data centers, water infrastructure and tribal relations, with several debates in late September and early October. Ahlers has pushed affordability as a defining issue, but there is little sign of a competitive race: fundraising details are sparse, Democratic exposure in the state is limited, and the structural environment strongly favors the incumbent party. A double-digit Republican win is the expected outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0185, "margin": -14.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0209, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0249, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0252, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.012, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0137, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0268, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0157, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -14.0}]}